Record service process memory in get-stats.py

performance.json cannot show how much memory a service uses: the
services figures are cgroup totals, which include page cache, and the
only processes it tracks are privsep, mysqld, erlang and etcd.

Also track uWSGI, oslo.service and neutron worker processes, and the
services that run a script with a config file in /etc, so that peak
and anonymous RSS per process show what an import change saves.

Prompt: Mikal asked for performance.json to record OpenStack service
processes, so that each import memory fix can be measured in CI.

